},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"Digital inspections make compliance enforceable. Powerfleet replaces paper forms with guided, digital pre‑shift checklists, ensures operators cannot bypass required steps, and can automatically restrict equipment access until inspections are completed. This helps organizations reach 100% regulatory compliance on required checks, with full audit trails.
","title":"2. How do we ensure pre‑shift inspections are actually completed — not rushed or skipped?"},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"Powerfleet verifies operator identity and certification status at the moment of use. Equipment remains locked until the operator meets training and certification requirements. This eliminates uncertified usage, prevents PIN sharing, and centralizes certification management for safer, more consistent operations.
","title":"3. How can we ensure only trained and certified operators use our equipment?"},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"With impact detection and event‑triggered video, Powerfleet captures WHEN, WHERE, and HOW each impact occurs. Supervisors get instant visibility to address root causes, coach operators, reduce damage rates by up to 80%, and prevent minor hits from compounding into major structural or inventory loss.
","title":"4. How do we identify the source of damage to racks, equipment, and product?"},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"
Powerfleet surfaces issues early with digital inspections and automated defect reporting, ensuring problems are found at the start of shifts, not mid‑operation. Maintenance teams receive real‑time alerts to prioritize repairs, reduce unplanned downtime, and stay ahead of equipment failures.
","title":"5. How do we reduce equipment downtime caused by missed defects or incomplete inspections?"},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"Many organizations over-lease equipment due to limited visibility into actual usage. Powerfleet provides utilization insights to identify over-capacity, return unnecessary rentals, and support data-driven capital decisions. Leaders gain the visibility needed to right-size fleets and reduce avoidable equipment costs.","title":"6. How can we right‑size our forklift fleet and reduce unnecessary rentals or leases?"},"type":"accordion_item"},{"props":{"content":"
